From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucas gelfond <lucasgelfond@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/29] demux: avformat: date the first packet of formats without timestamps

Raw formats flagged AVFMT_NOTIMESTAMPS (Shorten, OSQ, ...) hand out packets
without any timestamp when avformat has no parser for them. The audio
decoder drops everything until it sees a first timestamp and the clock never
gets a PCR, so these files open, read to the end and play nothing.

Date the first packet of such a track (and the first one after a seek) from
the current demuxer time; the decoder then counts samples from there.
---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/avformat/demux.c b/modules/demux/avformat/demux.c
--- a/modules/demux/avformat/demux.c
+++ b/modules/demux/avformat/demux.c
@@ -970,6 +970,18 @@ static int Demux( demux_t *p_demux )
     if( pkt.duration > 0 && p_frame->i_length <= 0 )
         p_frame->i_length = FROM_AVSCALE( pkt.duration, p_stream->time_base );
 
+    /* Formats without timestamps (raw Shorten, ...) may have no parser to
+     * make them up either. The decoder waits for a first timestamp and the
+     * clock for a PCR, so date the first packet of the track (again after
+     * a seek): the decoder counts samples from there. */
+    if( (p_sys->ic->iformat->flags & AVFMT_NOTIMESTAMPS) &&
+        p_frame->i_dts == VLC_TICK_INVALID && p_frame->i_pts == VLC_TICK_INVALID &&
+        p_track->i_pcr == VLC_TICK_INVALID )
+    {
+        p_frame->i_dts = p_frame->i_pts = VLC_TICK_0 +
+            (p_sys->i_pcr != VLC_TICK_INVALID ? p_sys->i_pcr : 0);
+    }
+
     /* Add here notoriously bugged file formats/samples */
     if( !strcmp( p_sys->fmt->name, "flv" ) )
     {
